09:45 < jonatack> As for grant KPIs, I don't think those credits make any difference in the overall scheme of things. At least not when I review grant applications and reports. If you were already a reviewer of the PR in question, which would generally be the case, that's enough ;)
09:46 < lightlike> well, at least in the gray areas. In clear cases where someone actually wrote most of the code of a commit, I think they should at least be co-author, if not first author, and I wouldn't think it rude to ask for it.
09:46 < jonatack> I look much, more more at the quality/value of the review.
